eep into the big names let's go  back to the beginning where i  first heard about this story it all  starts with super maxie a small  australian siege youtuber the way he  explains it about a month ago he woke up  to people in his discord freaking out  in an email from ubisoft saying that  somebody had logged into his account  under a new device  in the uk and he basically says that's  impossible i live in australia and i've  never been to the uk and on top of that  when he logged into his uplay account to  try to play  siege he got met with a message that's  saying this account has been permanently  banned  but um yeah i get up and jump on  my computer and open up siege and sure  enough i've got that message that  i've been well first off i log on to  steam and it's like you've been  permanently banned from  rainbow six siege right and i'm like oh  damn what the hell so i jump on  and i get the band message and i'm just  like  sorry i don't freak out or anything like  that i'm like oh okay there's been a  mistake  he went back and forth with ubisoft's  support for a while but they basically  said  hey the decision is final nothing is  going to change here  and to this day almost a month later his  account  is still banned he took to reddit to  explain the situation and out of sheer  desperation  he even emailed the ceo of ubisoft yves  gilman to explain what happened  nothing worked super maxi believes that  his account was hacked  the security measures were reset emails  and passwords all  changed and ubisoft just doesn't believe  that it wasn't him  and so i emailed him and i was just like  please like you know i told him about  myself i really tried to like  personalize and be like you know look  you know as  a fellow lover of the game which i'm  sure you love the game that you've  created  you know i'm sure that you um are  passionate about this community and  everything like that  i'm not trying to start beef i'm not  trying to start a war with you  i just want my account back and that'll  be the end of it like that's literally  all i want and instead of emailing me  back  or anything like that um i just got an  extra line  in my next support response message  which was in response to your email to  yves  and then was just like nope we've we've  fully investigated it and we believe  that you cheated  for him having his account banned means  he's lost a main source of  income and on top of that a portion of  his community  now believes that he could be a cheater  now originally when i heard about this  story i thought it was a shitty one-off  an anomaly that ended with this guy  probably getting screwed  but if we jump ahead a few weeks this  same problem is now happening to some of  the gigantic names i mentioned  earlier pengu king george nbk macy j  seph all of their accounts have been  hacked in a similar way  now while i interviewed bikini for this  story and you'll be hearing a lot of his  perspective here  i did confirm with a lot of the other  people involved that what he describes  is pretty much the same thing that  happened with them  the way bikini explains it he went to  bed the night of his birthday  and everything was great uh i wake up  um check twitter uh and uh yes  ironic had sent me a message like uh he  had received a message on uplay from my  account  uh with a new profile picture and  everything and it said the n word to him  and he said like uh dude  have you been hacked and then he sent a  picture of macy's r6 tab he realized  that macy had had his name  changed as well uh so he realized that  you know it was another one of these  hacker waves because it wasn't the first  time that this guy had done this  uh a month ago pengu was the target and  bk  were hacked three times in a week i  believe  yeah um so the fact that this has been  going on for a month  and and nothing has happened around this  is crazy and i i think this one was the  worst  so yeah the next morning after talking  to his ironic 